refute.evidence:
apps/web-app/src/services/api-service-wrapper.ts: the initialized field is at line 183 and its only write, inside the .then() callback, is at 207. isInitialized is at 221-227, formatPrice at 235-242 (delegates to CoreAPIService.formatPrice), and getPriceData at 250-259 (delegates to getInstance().getPriceData).

A git grep for 'APIService.(formatPrice|getPriceData|isInitialized)' and 'APIService[' across apps and packages found three kinds of hit:
- callers only in apps/web-app/src/services/__tests__/api-service-wrapper.test.ts;
- a comment at market-board-service.ts:475, plus another in market-board-service.test.ts:496;
- the core package's own APIService (APIService.test.ts, README), which is a different class and is untouched.

The other formatPrice and isInitialized hits are unrelated symbols:
- formatPrice in gradient-tool, mixer-tool, v4/result-card, MarketBoard and market-board-service;
- isInitialized in base-component, language-service, theme-service and WorldService.isInitialized.

Production uses of APIService are index.ts:126 (getInstance().getAPIStatus), market-board-service.ts:108 and :435 (getInstance and clearCache), and auth-service.ts:772 (clearCache). market-board-service.test.ts mocks api-service-wrapper with its own formatPrice, so removing the real method does not affect that mock.

Searches of apps/stoat-worker and apps/web-app/e2e found no references. Nothing uses a computed key or a window debug hook to reach these methods. The class is not exported through a package exports map, because web-app is an app. Web-app's coverage thresholds are global ratchets, and the removal takes out source and tests together. The fix also keeps resetInstance and the .then() debug log, which other tests still use.

